    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> declared independence in 1918 and won it in the War of Independence, confirmed by the Treaty of Tartu in 1920.</li><li>Occupied by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1940, it was restored in 1991 as the legal continuation of the pre-war republic.</li><li>Since 2004 it has been a member of the EU and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>, known worldwide for e-government and internet voting.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 2007 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> became the first country to allow online voting nationwide in a parliamentary election, using its national electronic ID card.</p></aside>
    </section>

